n":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T19:19:07.694513","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<table class=\"dataframe\">\n","<caption>A data.frame: 4 × 3</caption>\n","<thead>\n","\t<tr><th scope=col>member_casual</th><th scope=col>day_type</th><th scope=col>ride_id</th></tr>\n","\t<tr><th scope=col>&lt;chr&gt;</th><th scope=col>&lt;chr&gt;</th><th scope=col>&lt;int&gt;</th></tr>\n","</thead>\n","<tbody>\n","\t<tr><td>casual</td><td>Weekday</td><td>1476094</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>member</td><td>Weekday</td><td>2615958</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>casual</td><td>Weekend</td><td> 860581</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>member</td><td>Weekend</td><td> 850046</td></tr>\n","</tbody>\n","</table>\n"],"text/latex":["A data.frame: 4 × 3\n","\\begin{tabular}{lll}\n"," member\\_casual & day\\_type & ride\\_id\\\\\n"," <chr> & <chr> & <int>\\\\\n","\\hline\n","\t casual & Weekday & 1476094\\\\\n","\t member & Weekday & 2615958\\\\\n","\t casual & Weekend &  860581\\\\\n","\t member & Weekend &  850046\\\\\n","\\end{tabular}\n"],"text/markdown":["\n","A data.frame: 4 × 3\n","\n","| member_casual &lt;chr&gt; | day_type &lt;chr&gt; | ride_id &lt;int&gt; |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| casual | Weekday | 1476094 |\n","| member | Weekday | 2615958 |\n","| casual | Weekend |  860581 |\n","| member | Weekend |  850046 |\n","\n"],"text/plain":["  member_casual day_type ride_id\n","1 casual        Weekday  1476094\n","2 member        Weekday  2615958\n","3 casual        Weekend   860581\n","4 member        Weekend   850046"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["weekday_weekend <- aggregate(\n","  ride_id ~ member_casual + day_type,\n","  data = clean_trips_data3,\n","  FUN = length\n",")\n","\n","weekday_weekend"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":65,"id":"e4595d40","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-17T19:19:10.943841Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-17T19:19:10.942327Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-17T19:19:12.58071Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-17T19:19:12.57895Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.67365,"end_time":"2026-08-17T19:19:12.583111","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T19:19:10.909461","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["        \n","          Weekday  Weekend\n","  casual 63.17070 36.82930\n","  member 75.47475 24.52525"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["prop.table(\n","  table(\n","    clean_trips_data3$member_casual,\n","    clean_trips_data3$day_type\n","  ),\n","  margin = 1\n",") * 100"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"536f2211","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.030565,"end_time":"2026-08-17T19:19:12.64452","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T19:19:12.613955","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<h2 id=\"conclusion\">Conclusion</h2>\n","\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"019e5d3e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.031164,"end_time":"2026-08-17T19:19:12.706768","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T19:19:12.675604","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["\n","\n"," **KEY FINDINGS AND RECOMMENDATIONS**\n"," **Findings:**\n","\n","  **1:** Casual riders generally take longer rides than members. The typical casual ride lasts approximately 12.7 minutes compared with 8.7 minutes for members, while the average rises to 25.2 and 12.5 minutes respectively due to longer-duration trips.\n","\n","**2:** Casual riders demonstrate stronger weekend usage, suggesting their relationship with Cyclistic may be more leisure-oriented, whereas members show stronger and more consistent weekday usage.\n","\n","**3:** Casual riders showed a stronger preference for electric bikes, which accounted for approximately 54.5% of their rides. Member usage was more evenly distributed between classic and electric bikes, with classic bikes slightly more popular.\n","\n","**4:** Casual riders take their longest rides on weekends, averaging approximately 28–29 minutes, while member ride durations remain relatively consistent throughout the week at approximately 12–14 minutes.\n","\n","**5** Member rides show pronounced morning and evening peaks, particularly around 7–8 AM and 4–6 PM. Casual riders show a more gradual increase throughout the day, peaking around 5 PM, with casual usage exceeding member usage during the late-night hours.\n","\n","**6** 36.8% of casual rides occur on weekends vs 24.5% of member rides.\n","\n","   **Recomendations**\n","   \n","a: Since members ride less on the weekends, the company should run a special promotion exclusive for the members only.This will allow them to take more rides over the weekend.\n","   \n","b: Offer casual riders weekend only membership-promotions , so that the they have an experience of the membership benefits on the days, they take more rides. As long as the offer is lucrative , the company will see casual riders subscribing for membership.\n","      \n","c: Offer casual riders weekdays discounts .With this campaign the aim is to offer casual riders a discount or lucrative deal if they ride on weekdays.\n","  \n","d: Members ride for less periods due to the fact that, From the visual they ride for the same average duration between Monday and Friday.Which is a routine during the week, for commuting. This explains how they differ with casual riders who seem to be doing it for leisure other than commuting. Due to this l recommend a campaign which shows how biking can be fun for leisure , this should be targeted at the members. The campaign should cover how members can enjoy biking with their loved ones on a weekend\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e01ba6b0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.031252,"end_time":"2026-08-17T19:19:12.768976","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T19:19:12.737724","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["FOR MORE VISUALS I WILL USE POWER BI"]}],"metadata":{"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":6360852}],"dockerImageVersionId":30515,"isInterne